--TEST--
`$x is $cls` is refused, because the right-hand side of `is` is a type and a variable names a value — `instanceof` is the dynamic class test (`rule:types/type-test`, `rule:types/class-reference-sites`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The refusal that keeps the spelling free. PHP's Pattern Matching RFC
// binds a variable in this position
// (`rule:php-migration/is-takes-pattern-matchings-type-patterns`), so `is`
// cannot quietly read one as a class name here and stay compatible with the
// RFC we implement a row of.
class Animal {}

mixed $pet = new Animal();
string $cls = "Animal";
echo $pet is $cls, "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0812]: the right-hand side of `is` is a type, not a value
%A
error: aborting due to 1 error
